Actually, as someone said, I think there are more or less 2 kind of "gaze  
attack". One is passive and a mere look at the monster should activate it  
(Medusa). The other is active and the monster as to explicitely use it  
(pyrolisk, Umber Hulk). The first kind can be prevented (only) by wearing  
a blindfold, the second cannot. But the second kind should probably be  
reflected (bounce somewhere else ?) by reflection. Mirrors can probably  
send both kind to the monster since you're supposed to apply it correctly.  
Of course, some monsters could be protected from their own gaze. And  
shield of reflection should be 'a'pllyable as mirrors to keep consitancy  
with the legend.

